// End-to-end C++-interop coverage. Each section exercises one path of the C++ interop
// pipeline; on failure the section's exit code identifies which one regressed.
//   Trivially copyable C++ records by value - layout (size, alignment, packed,
//     over-aligned) checked against the C++ side's own sizeof/alignof, then round trips
//     through every AArch64 arrangement clang picks: coerced small integer, two-eightbyte,
//     HFA in float registers, indirect + sret.
//   C++ class members - instance methods (const and mutating, with arguments), static
//     methods, static data member reads, dispatch through a pointer receiver, the
//     const-overload ruling (an lvalue picks the non-const leg), and qualified scoped-enum
//     spellings. Access control and polymorphism are covered by Test/errors/err_cpp_*.cb.
//   C++ inheritance and VIRTUAL dispatch - polymorphic classes laid out from clang (vptr
//     slot + base subobjects), virtual calls through the vtable slot ItaniumVTableContext
//     assigned, virtual destructor via the Itanium deleting-destructor slot, and multiple
//     inheritance with a non-primary base whose `this` must be adjusted.
//   C++ NONTRIVIAL class lifetime - construction into the declared slot (`T(args)`),
//     copy/move construction, copy/move assignment, exactly-once destruction on normal
//     exit, nested scopes, early return, break and continue, nontrivial by-value arguments
//     (copy and move) and by-value returns constructed straight into the local, plus
//     new/delete and `unique T*` through the C++ operators. Every assertion is an EXACT
//     instrumented count, so an extra copy or a missed destructor fails here.
//   HEADER-ONLY C++ - inline free functions (including one that calls another, and one with
//     a static local), an all-inline nontrivial class, inline static data members as
//     lifetime counters, and an all-inline VIRTUAL hierarchy with no key function. Nothing
//     here has an out-of-line symbol, so every assertion also proves clang's definition
//     emission landed in the linked image. Two import groups cover the same code, so a
//     duplicate definition would fail the link instead of merging by ODR.
//   C++ interop via `import cpp` - namespaced/overloaded declarations.
//   C++ operator(), unary ~, and conversion operators bound by mangled linkage name,
//     reference params and returns as pointers, extern "C" bare linkage, nested namespaces,
//     widening and narrow-unsigned round trips, scoped-enum params, records by pointer.
//     Primitives and bare pointers only.
//   A refused callback ABI plan does not abort the header import.
//   A constructor binds a primitive pointer spelled as a CFlat synonym.
//   A default-argument wrapper for a function returning a record.
//   An unreferenced inline body calling an undefined symbol is dropped before the link; its
//     inline neighbour still binds and runs.
//   Member default-argument wrappers for const instance and static methods, including
//     full-argument and omitted-default calls.
//   An opaque union field preserves the size/alignment of an unrequested class-template
//     specialization when the enclosing record is returned.
//   Free C++ operator overloads are found through the operand namespace, including a nested
//     namespace, and compound assignment falls back to '+'.
//   A C++ reference return bound to a CFlat pointer local with no '&', in the declaration and
//     the assignment form, and proven to alias the referent rather than a copy.
//   Fixed-array pointer ABI, bool and class-typed member defaults, record conversion
//     through an initializer_list wrapper, and a class const-reference return copied into a
//     local.
//   The full C++ operator grid. cppi.Ops carries every MEMBER form (binary, compound,
//     unary, subscript, call, conversion, <=> and the relational operators C++20 rewrites
//     from it, && and ||), and cppi.opsfree.FreeOps the same list as FREE functions, plus
//     the reversed candidates (`int == Ops`, `RevOther == Rev`), `*`/`->` forwarding, and
//     `OpsSink << FreeOps`, whose left operand lives in another namespace.
//   Virtual members whose vtable SLOT cflat cannot name, and the CONSTRUCTION of a class
//     with virtual bases through a placement-new thunk. The covariant return and
//     virtual-base destructor use clang-synthesized thunks; adjacent guards pin the
//     existing base-record fallback and exact by-value resource counts.
//   Implicit scalar-to-class reference conversion, chained nontrivial class return
//     receivers, member reference arguments/defaults, and RAII.
//   C++ exceptions caught at the `program` boundary, including a two-frame CFlat call chain
//     and a normal program run afterward.
//   Namespace-scope C++ OBJECTS - out-of-line extern scalars, class-typed objects and const
//     ones, nested and inline namespaces, a global-scope object, header-only constants that
//     need their own storage, and a write through a mutable one.
//     Test/errors/err_cpp_namespace_const_assign.cb covers the rejected writes.
//   Imported mixed-type C++ bitfields follow Itanium allocation units; overflow still
//     splits, short/int and bool/int use the widest unit, and same-type runs preserve their
//     existing layout.
//   Unnamed zero-width C++ bitfields close an allocation unit under both same-type and
//     mixed-type neighbours; fields and sizeof agree with C++.
//   Class-scope `static const` with an in-class initializer and no out-of-line definition -
//     folded by value across int/unsigned/long long/bool/char/plain and scoped enum, a
//     chained initializer, a nested class, a member that also has an out-of-line
//     definition, use as an array bound and a switch case, and the constexpr /
//     inline-const / out-of-line neighbours that already bound.
//   C++ scoped-enum identity in free/member overload matching, converting constructors,
//     references, explicit casts, templates, and measured preservation of unscoped enum
//     conversions.
//   C++ REFERENCE data members - a `T&` / `T&&` / `T*&` member bound as a pointer field
//     (layout, by-value return and argument, direct construction, reads through the
//     referent), in a base class, in a class template specialization, and in an array
//     element. Reseating the field is refused;
//     Test/errors/err_cpp_reference_member_reseat.cb pins the message.
// `import cpp` selects C++ mode; the extension is irrelevant (the fixture header is a plain
// .h). The header supplies the declarations, the .cpp is compiled by the host C++ driver
// and linked in. Both are needed: the header alone has no definitions, and the source alone
// would not exercise the header-extraction path.
//   A C++ field whose type is a CLASS - a nested member class (one and two levels, an array
//     of them, a pointer to one, and one pointing back at its owner), a class-template
//     specialization spelled directly and through an alias, a specialization over the
//     owner's own nested class, and one whose template has a nontrivial destructor that the
//     owner's destruction must run. Each of these was embedded as opaque bytes, so every
//     member access failed.
//   A C++ CONSTRUCTOR parameter declared `T&` binds the ARGUMENT's address. Every argument
//     shape (a named local, `*ptr`, a CFlat struct field, an array element, `new T(*p)`), a
//     `const T&` given an lvalue and a prvalue temporary, a reference DATA MEMBER that must
//     alias the argument, a scalar `int&` parameter, a NON-COPYABLE referent, and
//     std.lock_guard / std.unique_lock over a CFlat-owned std.mutex proved by try_lock.
//     Each leg asserts the referent's value AFTER the constructed object was destroyed.
//     Every one of them received a bitwise `%ctor.refarg` stack COPY, so the ctor's writes
//     were lost and the dtor wrote through a dangling pointer.
//   Array ELEMENTS of a C++ class are default-CONSTRUCTED - `T[N] a = default;`, no
//     initializer, `= {}`, two dimensions, a nontrivial ctor with a TRIVIAL dtor, a
//     polymorphic element called virtually, a CFlat struct field of array type, `new T[n]`
//     at constant and runtime extent, a SHORT positional list whose unlisted tail must
//     still be constructed, a per-element brace list (plain and polymorphic), and a struct
//     field whose array default is a non-empty brace list. ONE code per SHAPE: each leg
//     folds the constructor count, the constructor's own invariant and the matching
//     destructor count under a single code. A fully trivial element keeps the whole-array
//     zeroinitializer. Test/errors/err_cpp_array_no_default_ctor.cb pins the
//     deleted-default-constructor refusal, including through the brace and short-tail
//     spellings.
//   C++ using-directives. A directive whose nominated namespace is NESTED INSIDE the
//     nominating one (one level and two, plus the member reached through it) rewrote its own
//     output forever and hung the compiler; the accept set around it - sibling nomination, a
//     two-hop chain, a cycle resolved from both ends, and a namespace nominating itself -
//     must still resolve. Test/errors/err_cpp_usingns_unknown.cb pins the diagnostic for a
//     name that exists through no directive.
//   C++ FREE OPERATOR TEMPLATES. libc++ declares every std.string binary operator as a free
//     function template over basic_string, so none was published or instantiated for concrete
//     operands: `+ == != < > <= >=` are covered for string/string, string/literal and
//     literal/string, with the result used as an initializer, as a condition, as a C++ call
//     argument and read back byte-wise. cpp_interop_freeoptpl.h repeats the shape in a header
//     the fixture owns (a class template with tagged free operator templates, a second one
//     declaring only == and <=> so the relational forms are C++20 rewrites, two
//     specializations, and a plain class with NON-template free operators as the accept set).

import cpp "library/cpp_interop_basic.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_basic.cpp" cache;
// Inheritance and virtual dispatch. Definitions are out-of-line on purpose - every
// virtual function needs a real symbol and the vtable needs a key function.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_poly.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_poly.cpp" cache;
// HEADER-ONLY C++ - no .cpp anywhere. Every definition is inline in the header, so
// clang CodeGen has to emit the bodies, vtables and inline statics into the companion module.
// The second header re-includes the first from a DIFFERENT import group, which is the
// duplicate-definition (ODR merge) check.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_inline.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_inline_again.h" cache;
// The `T&` constructor-parameter checks lock a CFlat-owned std.mutex through std.lock_guard / std.unique_lock.
import cpp "mutex" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_throw.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_scoped_enum.h" cache;
// C++ REFERENCE data members - bound as pointer fields, never reseatable.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_ref_member.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_field.h" cache;
// Array elements of a C++ class. Imported WITHOUT the header cache so those checks
// does not depend on cache state.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_arrayelem.h";
import "cpp_interop_globals.cb";
// Using-directives, including ones nominating a namespace nested in the nominator.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_usingns.h" cache;
// A C++ CONSTRUCTOR parameter declared `T&` binds the argument's address.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_ctorref.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_freeoptpl.h" cache;
import cpp "string" cache;
import "list.cb";
import "thread.cb";
import "malloc_allocator.cb";

// CFlat structs whose FIELD is a fixed array of a C++ class - `= default`, and a non-empty
// brace list over an element with a trivial and with a nontrivial destructor.
struct ArrElemHost { cppa.Trk[2] cells = default; };

// A CFlat struct field of C++ class type, used as a ctor `T&` argument.
struct CtorRefHost { cppcr.Cnt cell = default; };
struct ArrElemH5 { cppa.CtorOnly[2] cells = { v = 1 }; };
struct ArrElemH6 { cppa.Trk[2] cells = { v = 1 }; };
extern int strcmp(const char* a, const char* b);
int my_inc_cb(int x) { return x + 1; }
// Collision axis for the pointer-member section below: a FREE function named 'p', which the
// member name 'p' of cppi.ptrmem.Holder must not be resolved to.
int p(int x) { return x + 100; }
// Accept-set anchor: a CFlat struct holding a pointer to a C++ class already chained pre-fix.
struct PtrMemCflatHolder { cppi.ptrmem.Leaf* p = default; };
static bool near(double actual, double expected, double tol)
{
    double diff = actual - expected;
    if (diff < 0.0) { diff = -diff; }
    return diff <= tol;
}
// Nontrivial-lifetime helpers. Each holds a nontrivial C++ local and leaves through a DIFFERENT exit edge, so
// the counters below prove the existing cleanup paths (not a second mechanism) destroy it.
int life_early_return(int k)
{
    cppi.Tracked t = cppi.Tracked(k);
    if (k > 0) return t.value();
    return -1;
}
// A C++ class with VIRTUAL BASES held as a CFlat struct FIELD. Pre-fix this
// compiled and crashed on the first member call; the field was never constructed.
struct ThunkHolder { cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int> a = default; };
int cpp_throw_deep2(int value)
{
    return cppthrow.throw_if(value);
}

int cpp_throw_deep1(int value)
{
    return cpp_throw_deep2(value);
}
program CppThrowDirect
{
    int main(move list<string> args)
    {
        return cppthrow.throw_if(1);
    }
};

program CppThrowDeep
{
    int main(move list<string> args)
    {
        return cpp_throw_deep1(1);
    }
};

program CppThrowPlain
{
    int main(move list<string> args)
    {
        return cppthrow.throw_if(0) + cppthrow.plain(4);
    }
};
/*
 * M103: FILE-SCOPE globals of a C++ class with a nontrivial default constructor. Pre-fix every
 * one of these was a zeroinitializer that nothing ever constructed (gctor_count() == 0 and
 * gclsPoly.kind() segfaulted on the null vptr); the constructors now run from an
 * llvm.global_ctors entry before main. RULING: no exit-time destruction, so gdtor_count() == 0.
 */
cppa.GTrk gclsSingle = default;       // the plain '= default' spelling
cppa.GTrk gclsBare;                   // no initializer at all
cppa.GTrk gclsBrace = {};             // empty-brace value initialization
static cppa.GTrk gclsStatic = default;// 'static'-spelled file-scope global
cppa.GTrk[3] gclsArr3 = default;      // global ARRAY: one constructor per element
cppa.GTrk[2][2] gclsArr22 = default;  // every inner dimension counts
cppa.GPoly gclsPoly = default;        // the vptr slot was zero pre-fix
namespace GctNS { cppa.GTrk gclsNs = default; }   // inside a CFlat namespace
cppa.GSeq gclsSeqA = default;         // ORDER: the imported module's GSeq, then A, then B
cppa.GSeq gclsSeqB = default;
cppa.GProbe gclsProbe = default;      // its constructor READS a header-defined C++ static
// ACCEPT SET: a trivial C++ class stays a plain zero-init global with no init code (asserted in
// the IR, not by a value - zero IS its constructed value). It is declared here so that routing
// it into the module initializer by mistake would fail the LINK on a missing constructor symbol.
cppa.Plain gclsPlain = default;
extern int main()
{
    // ---- C++ exceptions at the program boundary -------------------------------------------------
    // Win64 keeps the existing SEH trampoline and does not emit the C++ guard.
    if const (__WINDOWS__) {
        return 0;
    }

    {
        CppThrowDirect direct;
        list<string> directArgs;
        direct.run(directArgs);
        direct.WaitForExit();
        if (direct.exitCode != -1) return 1554;

        CppThrowDeep deep;
        list<string> deepArgs;
        deep.run(deepArgs);
        deep.WaitForExit();
        if (deep.exitCode != -1) return 1555;

        // This normal run follows both throwing program threads in the same process.
        CppThrowPlain plain;
        list<string> plainArgs;
        plain.run(plainArgs);
        plain.WaitForExit();
        if (plain.exitCode != 5) return 1556;
    }

    // Keep one additional non-throwing run after the throwing objects have torn down.
    {
        CppThrowPlain plainAgain;
        list<string> argsAgain;
        plainAgain.run(argsAgain);
        plainAgain.WaitForExit();
        if (plainAgain.exitCode != 5) return 1557;
    }

    // C++ side of the long double round-trip from Section O.
    if (cppi.ld_identity(2.5) != 2.5)            return 148;
    if (cppi.ld_add(1.25, 2.5) != 3.75)         return 149;
    double cppDout = 0.0;
    cppi.ld_store(7.125, &cppDout);
    if (cppDout != 7.125)                        return 150;

    // ---- C++ interop via `import cpp`: namespaced and overloaded declarations -------------------
    // Namespaced call under the dotted CFlat spelling, bound to the Itanium/MSVC
    // mangled symbol. The double overload adds 1000, so the return value alone
    // proves WHICH overload was selected.
    if (cppi.add(40, 2) != 42)                   return 270;
    if (cppi.add(40.5, 2.0) != 1042)             return 271;

    // Nested namespace: every '::' prefix registers as a CFlat namespace.
    if (cppi.inner.twice(21) != 42)              return 272;

    // extern "C" inside a C++ translation unit keeps its bare linkage name and is
    // callable without a namespace qualifier.
    if (cppi_c_linkage(37) != 42)                return 273;

    // Reference parameter: spelled as a pointer on the CFlat side, so the call site
    // passes the address of a local explicitly. pick_ref writes 7 and returns the old
    // value, which makes the MUTATION observable, not just the argument transfer.
    int cppiRef = 5;
    if (cppi.pick_ref(&cppiRef) != 5)            return 274;
    if (cppiRef != 7)                            return 275;

    // const reference read: same pointer shape, no write-back.
    int cppiCRef = 41;
    if (cppi.read_cref(&cppiCRef) != 42)         return 276;
    if (cppiCRef != 41)                          return 277;

    // Reference RETURN arrives as an alias to the C++ side's storage.
    alias int cppiSlot = cppi.ref_slot();
    if (cppiSlot != 99)                          return 278;
    cppiSlot = 5;
    alias int cppiSlot2 = cppi.ref_slot();
    if (cppiSlot2 != 5)                          return 279;

    // Plain pointer parameter and return (no reference decay involved).
    int cppiVal = 9;
    int* cppiIdent = cppi.ptr_ident(&cppiVal);
    if (*cppiIdent != 9)                         return 280;

    // Widening: 'long long' return must keep all 64 bits, not truncate to i32.
    if (cppi.widen(3) != 3000000000)             return 281;
    if (cppi.widen(-3) != -3000000000)           return 282;

    // Narrow unsigned round trip: 'unsigned char' maps to u8 on both legs.
    if ((int)cppi.uc((u8)200) != 201)            return 283;
    if ((int)cppi.uc((u8)0) != 1)                return 284;

    // A scoped enum ('enum class Mode : int') parameter decays to int like a C enum,
    // so the declaration is published rather than skipped as an unsupported type.
    if (cppi.mode_value(1) != 10)                return 285;
    if (cppi.mode_value(0) != 0)                 return 286;

    // wchar_t is 16-bit on Windows and 32-bit elsewhere; the argument must be spelled at
    // the width the target maps it to.
    if const (__WINDOWS__) { if (cppi.wchar_roundtrip((u16)0x263a) != 0x263a) return 288; }
    else                   { if (cppi.wchar_roundtrip((i32)0x263a) != 0x263a) return 288; }
    if (cppi.char16_roundtrip((u16)0x263a) != 0x263a) return 289;
    if (cppi.char32_roundtrip((u32)0x1f642) != 0x1f642) return 323;
    if (cppi.small8_value(cppi.Small8.Value) != 200) return 324;
    if (cppi.small8_roundtrip(cppi.Small8.Value) != cppi.Small8.Value) return 325;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Small8Holder) != 2)       return 326;
    if (alignof(cppi.Small8Holder) != 1)      return 327;
    if (cppi.Dir.Left != 1 || cppi.dir_value(cppi.Dir.Left) != 1) return 328;

    cppi.Outer.Inner impInner = default;
    impInner.value = 21;
    if (impInner.twice() != 42)                 return 329;
    cppi.Outer.store = 7;
    if (cppi.Outer.store != 7)                 return 630;
    if (cppi.read_outer_store() != 7)          return 631;
    cppi.Outer.store = 11;
    if (cppi.read_outer_store() != 11)         return 632;
    if (cppi.Outer.store != 11)                return 633;
    if (cppi.Outer.Kind.A != 3)                return 619;
    cppi.Number impNumber = default;
    impNumber.i = 42;
    if (cppi.use_number(&impNumber) != 42)      return 621;
    cppi.AnonymousUnion impAnon = default;
    impAnon.__anon0.i = 9;
    if (impAnon.__anon0.i != 9)                 return 622;
    cppi.Bits impBits = default;
    impBits.a = 3; impBits.b = 4;
    if (cppi.use_bits(&impBits) != 34)          return 623;
    cppi.ArrayHolder impArray = default;
    impArray.arr[0] = 1; impArray.arr[1] = 2; impArray.arr[2] = 3; impArray.arr[3] = 4;
    if (cppi.use_array(&impArray) != 10)        return 624;

    cppi.Buf<int, 4> impBuf = default;
    if (impBuf.cap() != 4)                       return 625;
    cppi.Buf<int, cppi.Dir.Right> impEnumBuf = default;
    if (impEnumBuf.cap() != 2)                   return 631;

    if (cppi.scaled_default(10) != 30)          return 632;
    if (cppi.scaled_default(10, 4) != 40)       return 633;
    if (cppi.default_double_ptr() != 25)        return 634;
    int impDefaultMarker = 7;
    if (cppi.default_double_ptr(3.0, &impDefaultMarker) != 37) return 635;
    if (cppi.default_fn_arg(10) != 119)         return 750;
    if (cppi.default_fn_arg(10, my_inc_cb) != 20) return 751;
    if (cppi.default_fn_arg(10, my_inc_cb, 4) != 15) return 752;
    int[3] impDefaultArray = {4, 5, 6};
    if (cppi.default_array_arg(1) != 16)         return 753;
    if (cppi.default_array_arg(1, impDefaultArray) != 25) return 754;
    if (cppi.default_array_arg(1, impDefaultArray, 4) != 20) return 755;
    cppi.Point impDefaultPoint = default;
    impDefaultPoint.x = 2; impDefaultPoint.y = 3;
    if (impDefaultPoint.mode_scaled() != 5)      return 636;



    cppi.IntArray4 impArrayTemplate = default;
    impArrayTemplate[0] = 8; impArrayTemplate[1] = 9;
    if (impArrayTemplate.size() != 4 || impArrayTemplate[0] + impArrayTemplate[1] != 17) return 626;

    // A record is reachable by POINTER. Passing one BY VALUE is legal when the C++ type is
    // trivially copyable (below); a NONTRIVIAL one is refused - see
    // Test/errors/err_cpp_record_by_value.cb.
    cppi.Pair recPair = default;
    recPair.a = 40; recPair.b = 2;
    if (cppi.read_pair(&recPair) != 42)           return 287;

    // ---- trivially copyable records by value ----------------------------------------------------
    // Layout first. sizeof/alignof come back from the C++ side as functions, so any
    // disagreement between clang's layout and cflat's is a hard failure here rather than
    // a silent register mismatch inside the calls below.
    if (sizeof(cppi.Small)   != cppi.size_of(0))  return 290;
    if (alignof(cppi.Small)  != cppi.align_of(0)) return 291;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Mixed)   != cppi.size_of(1))  return 292;
    if (alignof(cppi.Mixed)  != cppi.align_of(1)) return 293;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Large)   != cppi.size_of(2))  return 294;
    if (alignof(cppi.Large)  != cppi.align_of(2)) return 295;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Hfa)     != cppi.size_of(3))  return 296;
    if (alignof(cppi.Hfa)    != cppi.align_of(3)) return 297;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Packed)  != cppi.size_of(4))  return 298;
    if (alignof(cppi.Packed) != cppi.align_of(4)) return 299;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Aligned) != cppi.size_of(5))  return 300;
    if (alignof(cppi.Aligned)!= cppi.align_of(5)) return 301;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Pair)    != cppi.size_of(6))  return 302;
    // The packed record is the sharpest layout check: 5 bytes, alignment 1.
    if (sizeof(cppi.Packed) != 5)                 return 303;
    if (alignof(cppi.Packed) != 1)                return 304;
    if (sizeof(cppi.Aligned) != 32)               return 305;

    // Two bytes, coerced into ONE register wider than the record itself.
    cppi.Small recSmall = default;
    recSmall.a = -5; recSmall.b = (u8)200;
    cppi.Small recSmallOut = cppi.small_bump(recSmall);
    if ((int)recSmallOut.a != -4)                  return 306;
    if ((int)recSmallOut.b != 201)                 return 307;

    // 16 bytes of mixed FP/integer: two 8-byte chunks, NOT an HFA.
    cppi.Mixed recMixed = default;
    recMixed.d = 2.5; recMixed.i = 41;
    cppi.Mixed recMixedOut = cppi.mixed_bump(recMixed);
    if (!near(recMixedOut.d, 3.5, 1e-12))          return 308;
    if (recMixedOut.i != 42)                       return 309;

    // 24 bytes: indirect in, hidden sret out.
    cppi.Large recLarge = default;
    recLarge.x = 10; recLarge.y = 20; recLarge.z = 30;
    cppi.Large recLargeOut = cppi.large_bump(recLarge);
    if (recLargeOut.x != 11)                       return 310;
    if (recLargeOut.y != 21)                       return 311;
    if (recLargeOut.z != 31)                       return 312;

    // Homogeneous float aggregate: four separate float registers under AAPCS64.
    cppi.Hfa recHfa = default;
    recHfa.a = 1.0f; recHfa.b = 2.0f; recHfa.c = 3.0f; recHfa.d = 4.0f;
    cppi.Hfa recHfaOut = cppi.hfa_bump(recHfa);
    if (!near((double)recHfaOut.a, 2.0, 1e-6))     return 313;
    if (!near((double)recHfaOut.b, 3.0, 1e-6))     return 314;
    if (!near((double)recHfaOut.c, 4.0, 1e-6))     return 315;
    if (!near((double)recHfaOut.d, 5.0, 1e-6))     return 316;

    // Packed: the coercion must read exactly 5 bytes with 'n' at byte offset 1.
    cppi.Packed recPacked = default;
    recPacked.c = (u8)7; recPacked.n = 1000;
    cppi.Packed recPackedOut = cppi.packed_bump(recPacked);
    if ((int)recPackedOut.c != 8)                  return 317;
    if (recPackedOut.n != 1001)                    return 318;

    // Over-aligned: indirect both ways, with a 32-byte-aligned temp and sret slot.
    cppi.Aligned recAligned = default;
    recAligned.x = 100; recAligned.y = 200;
    cppi.Aligned recAlignedOut = cppi.aligned_bump(recAligned);
    if (recAlignedOut.x != 101)                    return 319;
    if (recAlignedOut.y != 201)                    return 320;

    // A scalar WEDGED between two aggregates whose slots consume different register counts:
    // s -> one coerced register, k -> one integer register, l -> one hidden pointer.
    if (cppi.mixed_args(recSmall, 3, recLarge) != -2999640) return 321;

    // By-value and by-pointer records in the same signature.
    if (cppi.pair_and_small(&recPair, recSmall) != 237) return 322;

    // ---- C++ class members ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // A trivially copyable class carries no lifetime obligations, so these checks isolate
    // member binding: 'this' passing, argument marshalling, static members, and the
    // const-overload ruling.
    cppi.Point memP = default;
    memP.x = 3; memP.y = 4;

    // const instance method: 'this' is the receiver's address, result comes back in a register.
    if (memP.sum() != 7)                          return 330;

    // Mutating instance method: the write must land in the CALLER's storage, not a copy.
    memP.bump(2);
    if (memP.x != 5)                              return 331;
    if (memP.y != 6)                              return 332;
    if (memP.sum() != 11)                         return 333;

    // Two arguments after 'this'.
    if (memP.scaled(2, 1) != 23)                  return 334;
    char* memOut = nullptr;
    memP.set_out(memOut);
    if (memOut == nullptr || strcmp(memOut, "set-out") != 0) return 344;

    // const/non-const overload pair on an LVALUE receiver: the RULING says the NON-const leg
    // wins, and it is the leg that returns 1.
    if (memP.probe() != 1)                        return 335;

    // Static method: no receiver, called through the dotted type name.
    if (cppi.Point.origin_sum() != 0)            return 336;

    // Static data member READ. bump() incremented it exactly once above.
    if (cppi.Point.s_calls != 1)                 return 337;
    memP.bump(0);
    if (cppi.Point.s_calls != 2)                 return 338;

    // Same dispatch through a POINTER receiver.
    cppi.Point* memQ = &memP;
    if (memQ.sum() != 11)                         return 339;
    memQ.bump(1);
    if (memP.x != 6)                              return 340;

    // A public method that reads a PRIVATE field is fine; naming the field is not - see
    // Test/errors/err_cpp_private_member.cb.
    if (memP.hidden() != 0)                       return 341;

    // A scoped enum nested in a namespace is also published under its QUALIFIED C++ spelling,
    // so the enumerator can be written the way C++ writes it instead of as a bare integer.
    if (cppi.Mode.On != 1)                       return 342;
    if (cppi.mode_value(cppi.Mode.On) != 10)     return 343;

    // ---- nontrivial C++ class lifetime ----------------------------------------------------------
    // cppi.Tracked increments an exported counter in every special member, so each check below
    // is an EXACT count: one extra copy, one missed destructor, or a double destruction fails.

    // Simple scope: one construction, one destruction, nothing else.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked t = cppi.Tracked(5);
        if (t.value() != 5)                      return 350;
        if (cppi.dtor_count() != 0)              return 351;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 352;
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 0)                  return 353;
    if (cppi.move_count() != 0)                  return 354;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 355;

    // Nested scopes: the inner object dies at the inner brace, the outer one at the outer brace.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked outer = cppi.Tracked(1);
        {
            cppi.Tracked inner = cppi.Tracked(2);
            if (inner.value() != 2)              return 356;
            if (cppi.dtor_count() != 0)          return 357;
        }
        if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)              return 358;
        if (outer.value() != 1)                  return 359;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 2)                  return 360;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 361;

    // Early return out of a helper that holds one.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    if (life_early_return(4) != 4)                 return 362;
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 363;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 364;

    // break: three iterations ran, three objects were destroyed (including the one live at break).
    cppi.reset_counts();
    for (int lifeI = 0; lifeI < 5; lifeI++)
    {
        cppi.Tracked t = cppi.Tracked(lifeI);
        if (t.value() != lifeI)                    return 365;
        if (lifeI == 2) break;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 3)                  return 366;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 3)                  return 367;

    // continue: the object is destroyed on the continue edge as well as the fall-through edge.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    for (int lifeJ = 0; lifeJ < 4; lifeJ++)
    {
        cppi.Tracked t = cppi.Tracked(lifeJ);
        if (lifeJ % 2 == 0) continue;
        if (t.value() != lifeJ)                    return 368;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 4)                  return 369;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 4)                  return 370;

    // Copy construction from a T lvalue: exactly one copy, no move, both objects destroyed.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked src = cppi.Tracked(11);
        cppi.Tracked dst = src;
        if (dst.value() != 11)                   return 371;
        if (src.value() != 11)                   return 372;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 373;
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 1)                  return 374;
    if (cppi.move_count() != 0)                  return 375;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 376;

    // Move construction: the source is compile-time consumed (reading it is an error - see
    // Test/errors/err_cpp_use_after_move.cb) but STILL destroyed, so BOTH objects are destroyed.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked from = cppi.Tracked(12);
        cppi.Tracked to = move from;
        if (to.value() != 12)                    return 377;
    }
    if (cppi.move_count() != 1)                  return 378;
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 0)                  return 379;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 380;

    // Copy assignment over a LIVE object: the C++ operator runs, never a byte store.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked a = cppi.Tracked(1);
        cppi.Tracked b = cppi.Tracked(2);
        b = a;
        if (b.value() != 1)                      return 381;
        if (cppi.copy_assign_count() != 1)       return 382;
        if (cppi.copy_count() != 0)              return 383;
    }
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 384;

    // Move assignment consumes the source and leaves it destructible.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked a = cppi.Tracked(3);
        cppi.Tracked b = cppi.Tracked(4);
        b = move a;
        if (b.value() != 3)                      return 385;
        if (cppi.move_assign_count() != 1)       return 386;
    }
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 387;

    // By-value ARGUMENT: the caller copy-constructs a temp, the callee reads it, the temp is
    // destroyed - so one copy and two destructions in total.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked a = cppi.Tracked(6);
        if (cppi.take_tracked(a) != 6)           return 388;
    }
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 1)                  return 389;
    if (cppi.move_count() != 0)                  return 390;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 391;

    // By-value argument written `move x`: move-construction instead of a copy.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked a = cppi.Tracked(7);
        if (cppi.take_moved(move a) != 70)       return 392;
    }
    if (cppi.move_count() != 1)                  return 393;
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 0)                  return 394;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 2)                  return 395;

    // By-value RETURN into a local: constructed straight into the declared slot through the sret
    // pointer, so there is NO copy and NO move at all - one construction, one destruction.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked r = cppi.make_tracked(9);
        if (r.value() != 9)                      return 396;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 397;
    if (cppi.copy_count() != 0)                  return 398;
    if (cppi.move_count() != 0)                  return 399;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 400;

    // new / delete through the C++ global operators, never CFlat's allocator.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    cppi.Tracked* lifeP = new cppi.Tracked(13);
    if (lifeP.value() != 13)                       return 401;
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 402;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 0)                  return 403;
    delete lifeP;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 404;

    // `unique T*` composes: scope exit destroys AND frees through the same C++ operator pair.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        unique cppi.Tracked* lifeQ = new cppi.Tracked(14);
        if (lifeQ.value() != 14)                   return 405;
        if (cppi.dtor_count() != 0)              return 406;
    }
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 407;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 408;

    // A nontrivial result nobody declares a slot for is a TEMPORARY: it is still destroyed, once,
    // at the end of the full expression.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    _ = cppi.make_tracked(16);
    if (cppi.ctor_count() != 1)                  return 411;
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 412;

    // `_ = move x` releases NOW and must not destroy a second time at scope exit.
    cppi.reset_counts();
    {
        cppi.Tracked a = cppi.Tracked(15);
        _ = move a;
        if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)              return 409;
    }
    if (cppi.dtor_count() != 1)                  return 410;

    // ---- C++ inheritance and virtual dispatch ---------------------------------------------------
    // Every offset and vtable slot below is clang's own answer, cross-checked against
    // `clang++ -S -emit-llvm -O0` for the same calls: Shape::area is vtable slot 2, the deleting
    // destructor is slot 1, and Right sits at byte 16 of Both.

    // Layout: a polymorphic class is a REAL type whose size matches C++ exactly.
    if (sizeof(cpppoly.Shape) != 16)             return 420;
    // Circle's `radius` lands in Shape's tail padding under Itanium; the MS ABI never reuses it.
    if const (__WINDOWS__) { if (sizeof(cpppoly.Circle) != 24) return 421; }
    else                   { if (sizeof(cpppoly.Circle) != 16) return 421; }
    if (sizeof(cpppoly.Right) != 16)             return 422;
    if (sizeof(cpppoly.Both) != 32)              return 423;

    // Object built in C++: virtual dispatch through a BASE pointer picks the derived override,
    // the non-virtual method still binds directly, and the inherited field reads through.
    cpppoly.reset_poly_counts();
    cpppoly.Shape* virtC = cpppoly.make(0);        // a Circle
    if (virtC.area() != 50)                        return 424;   // Circle::area, radius 5
    if (virtC.plain() != 102)                      return 425;   // Shape::plain, non-virtual
    if (virtC.tag != 2)                            return 426;   // Circle's ctor set tag = 2
    // `delete` through the base pointer takes the vtable's DELETING destructor, so the DERIVED
    // destructor chain runs - Circle's, then Shape's - and the storage goes back to C++.
    delete virtC;
    if (cpppoly.circle_dtors() != 1)             return 427;
    if (cpppoly.shape_dtors() != 1)              return 428;
    if (cpppoly.square_dtors() != 0)             return 429;

    cpppoly.Shape* virtS = cpppoly.make(1);        // a Square
    if (virtS.area() != 49)                        return 430;   // Square::area, side 7
    cpppoly.destroy(virtS);                        // released on the C++ side
    if (cpppoly.square_dtors() != 1)             return 431;

    // Object constructed BY CFLAT on the stack: the C++ constructor writes the vptr, so the same
    // virtual dispatch works, and scope exit runs the derived destructor.
    cpppoly.reset_poly_counts();
    {
        cpppoly.Circle virtStack = default;
        if (virtStack.radius != 5)                 return 432;
        if (virtStack.tag != 2)                    return 433;
        // Shape::plain is INHERITED: it is registered on Circle too, with `this` retyped.
        if (virtStack.plain() != 102)              return 452;
        if (virtStack.area() != 50)                return 453;   // Circle's own override, direct
        cpppoly.Shape* virtBase = &virtStack;
        if (virtBase.area() != 50)                 return 434;
        if (virtBase.tag != 2)                     return 435;
    }
    if (cpppoly.circle_dtors() != 1)             return 436;
    if (cpppoly.shape_dtors() != 1)              return 437;

    // Object constructed BY CFLAT on the heap, then released through a BASE pointer.
    cpppoly.reset_poly_counts();
    cpppoly.Square* virtHeap = new cpppoly.Square();
    if (virtHeap.area() != 49)                     return 438;
    cpppoly.Shape* virtHeapBase = move virtHeap;
    if (virtHeapBase.area() != 49)                 return 439;
    delete virtHeapBase;
    if (cpppoly.square_dtors() != 1)             return 440;
    if (cpppoly.shape_dtors() != 1)              return 441;

    // MULTIPLE inheritance. Right is the NON-PRIMARY base of Both, at byte 16, so every
    // Both -> Right crossing must add 16; reading rv is what proves it happened.
    cpppoly.Both virtB = default;
    if (virtB.lv != 33)                            return 442;   // inherited from Left
    if (virtB.rv != 44)                            return 443;   // inherited from Right
    if (virtB.both_only() != 77)                   return 444;
    if (virtB.l() != 1033)                         return 445;   // Both::l overrides Left::l
    if (virtB.r() != 2044)                         return 446;   // Both::r overrides Right::r
    // C++ side takes a Right* and reads rv: wrong adjustment would hand it Left's storage.
    if (cpppoly.read_right(&virtB) != 44)          return 447;
    // C++ side dispatches virtually on that same adjusted pointer and lands on Both::r.
    if (cpppoly.call_right(&virtB) != 2044)        return 448;
    // The adjustment also happens on a STORE, so a saved base pointer is already correct.
    cpppoly.Right* virtR = &virtB;
    if (cpppoly.read_right(virtR) != 44)           return 449;
    if (virtR.rv != 44)                            return 450;
    if (virtR.r() != 2044)                         return 451;   // virtual, through Right's vtable
    // An override of a NON-PRIMARY base virtual, reached through a DERIVED pointer: the slot
    // must come from Both's own vtable (unadjusted this), not from Right's.
    cpppoly.Both* virtBp = &virtB;
    if (virtBp.r() != 2044)                        return 452;
    if (virtBp.l() != 1033)                        return 453;
    if (virtBp.both_only() != 77)                  return 454;

    // ---- class names containing a declarator keyword --------------------------------------------
    // "constant" contains "const" and "classBase" contains "class". Both are NON-PRIMARY bases
    // of QualNames, so a lost class identity shows up as a missing base adjustment.
    cpppoly.QualNames* virtQ = cpppoly.make_qual();
    if (cpppoly.read_constant(virtQ) != 66)        return 455;
    if (cpppoly.read_class_base(virtQ) != 77)      return 456;
    if (virtQ.cv != 66)                            return 457;
    if (virtQ.bv != 77)                            return 458;
    if (virtQ.l() != 3055)                         return 459;   // override of Left::l
    cpppoly.destroy_qual(virtQ);

    // ---- virtual members reached through a clang thunk ------------------------------------------
    /*
     * Under the MS ABI a member introduced by a NON-PRIMARY base sits in a vfptr at a non-zero
     * offset and one reached through a VIRTUAL base sits in a vfptr found through the vbtable;
     * MicrosoftVTableContext reports both as locations cflat cannot index. Most such members are
     * still reachable through the record of the base that DECLARES them, with `this` adjusted -
     * the guard legs below pin that path down, including its exact resource cost, because the
     * fix must not displace it. Two cases have no such fallback and are what the thunk exists
     * for: a DESTRUCTOR (only ever looked up on the class itself) and a COVARIANT return (whose
     * fallback hands back an unadjusted pointer, so it is wrong rather than merely slower).
     *
     * The shapes are TEMPLATE specializations on purpose: a directly named class with virtual
     * bases is refused at layout, so a specialization - held as a sized blob - is the only
     * spelling whose members reach the vtable-slot gate at all.
     */
    // Built on the C++ side: cflat cannot construct a class with virtual bases, and what is
    // under test here is the dispatch into one, not the construction of one.
    cpppoly.TwoSlots<int>* thunk = cpppoly.make_two_slots();
    // GUARD legs: these bind through the declaring base's record and already worked. They are
    // here so a wider thunk trigger, which would displace that path, fails loudly.
    if (cpppoly.read_slot(thunk) != 33)            return 1000;
    if (cpppoly.read_second(thunk) != 44)          return 1001;
    if (thunk.primary() != 1033)                   return 1002;   // primary vfptr, direct slot call
    if (thunk.second() != 2044)                    return 1003;   // non-primary vfptr
    if (thunk.second_add(3, 4) != 78)              return 1004;   // 44 + 3*10 + 4
    if (thunk.second_pure() != 3044)               return 1005;   // pure virtual, overridden

    // GUARD: a by-value class argument costs exactly one copy on BOTH vfptrs. A thunk in this
    // position would add a forwarding move and its destruction, and these counts would change.
    {
        cpppoly.SlotVal thunkV = cpppoly.SlotVal(5);
        cpppoly.reset_slot_counts();
        if (thunk.primary_val(thunkV) != 48)         return 1006;   // 33 + 5*3, primary vfptr
        if (cpppoly.slot_copies() != 1)          return 1007;
        if (cpppoly.slot_moves() != 0)           return 1008;
        if (cpppoly.slot_dtors() != 1)           return 1009;
        cpppoly.reset_slot_counts();
        if (thunk.second_val(thunkV) != 54)          return 1010;   // 44 + 5*2, non-primary vfptr
        if (cpppoly.slot_copies() != 1)          return 1011;
        if (cpppoly.slot_moves() != 0)           return 1012;
        if (cpppoly.slot_dtors() != 1)           return 1013;
    }

    // GUARD: a class RETURN by value is elided straight into the caller's local, on either path.
    cpppoly.reset_slot_counts();
    {
        cpppoly.SlotVal thunkR = thunk.second_ret();
        if (thunkR.v != 49)                        return 1014;   // 44 + 5
        if (cpppoly.slot_ctors() != 1)           return 1015;
        if (cpppoly.slot_copies() != 0)          return 1016;
        if (cpppoly.slot_moves() != 0)           return 1017;
        if (cpppoly.slot_dtors() != 0)           return 1018;
    }
    if (cpppoly.slot_dtors() != 1)               return 1019;
    cpppoly.destroy_two_slots(thunk);

    /*
     * COVARIANT return. The source read is a guard; the clone return and Slot read are independent
     * PRE discriminators for the unadjusted covariant result.
     */
    cpppoly.CloneDer<int>* thunkC = cpppoly.make_clone_der();
    // GUARD: PRE probe passed (exit 0); proves the source CloneDer value is valid.
    if (cpppoly.read_clone(thunkC) != 77)          return 1020;
    cpppoly.CloneDer<int>* thunkC2 = thunkC.clone();
    // DISCRIMINATOR: PRE probe exits 1021 at this read; the covariant result is unadjusted.
    if (cpppoly.read_clone(thunkC2) != 78)         return 1021;
    // DISCRIMINATOR: PRE probe exits 1022 at this read; the same result misses the Slot subobject.
    if (cpppoly.read_slot(thunkC2) != 66)          return 1022;
    cpppoly.destroy_clone(thunkC2);
    cpppoly.destroy_clone(thunkC);

    /*
     * VIRTUAL base. The t() and u() arms are independent PRE guards for existing fallback paths.
     * delete is a PRE discriminator: it leaves vbase_dtors at 0 without the destructor thunk.
     */
    cpppoly.VBaseUse<int>* thunkV2 = cpppoly.make_vbase_use();
    // GUARD: PRE probe passed (exit 0); protects the virtual-base method fallback.
    if (thunkV2.t() != 107)                        return 1023;
    // GUARD: PRE probe passed (exit 0); protects the derived-class virtual call.
    if (thunkV2.u() != 9)                          return 1024;
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    delete thunkV2;
    // DISCRIMINATOR: PRE probe exits 1025; delete leaves vbase_dtors at 0 without the thunk.
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 1)              return 1025;

    /*
     * VIRTUAL-BASE CONSTRUCTION. Each constructor of such a class binds to a clang-emitted
     * placement-new thunk, so clang - not cflat - passes the implicit most-derived flag / VTT.
     * Legs marked DISCRIMINATOR are refused outright by the pre-fix binary ("has no default
     * constructor cflat can call"); the GUARD legs are the accept-set the on-demand
     * variadic-constructor wrapper already served and that must keep working.
     */
    // DISCRIMINATOR: PRE binary refuses this declaration; the dtor count proves one object.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        cpppoly.VBaseUse<int> thunkD = default;
        if (thunkD.t() != 107)                     return 1026;   // 7 + 100, through the vbase
        if (thunkD.u() != 9)                       return 1027;
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 1)              return 1028;

    // GUARD: an explicit-argument constructor already worked through the wrapper path.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int> thunkA = cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int>(5);
        if (thunkA.a() != 5)                       return 1029;
        if (thunkA.t() != 107)                     return 1030;
        cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int> thunkA2 = cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int>(11, 12);
        if (thunkA2.t() != 111)                    return 1031;
        if (thunkA2.a() != 12)                     return 1032;
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 2)              return 1033;

    // DISCRIMINATOR: the DEFAULT constructor of a class that also declares others.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int> thunkA3 = default;
        if (thunkA3.a() != 1)                      return 1034;
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 1)              return 1035;

    // DISCRIMINATOR: TWO virtual bases. Both vbase subobjects must be reachable and adjusted.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        cpppoly.VBaseDiamond<int> thunkDm = default;
        if (thunkDm.t() != 13)                     return 1036;   // 3 + 10, first virtual base
        if (thunkDm.s() != 24)                     return 1037;   // 4 + 20, second virtual base
        if (thunkDm.d() != 5)                      return 1038;
        cpppoly.VBaseDiamond<int> thunkDm2 = cpppoly.VBaseDiamond<int>(9);
        if (thunkDm2.d() != 9)                     return 1039;
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 2)              return 1040;

    // DISCRIMINATOR: a class DERIVING from one with virtual bases. The most-derived flag is 1
    // for the complete object only, so the vbase is initialized exactly once.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        cpppoly.VBaseDer<int> thunkDr = default;
        if (thunkDr.t() != 102)                    return 1041;   // tv = 2, +100
        if (thunkDr.a() != 1003)                   return 1042;   // av = 3, +1000
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 2)              return 1043;   // ~VBaseDer then ~VBaseArgs

    // DISCRIMINATOR: the HEAP spelling. PRE binary reports "has no constructor taking 1
    // argument(s)" - the `new` site has no wrapper fallback, only the bound constructor list.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int>* thunkH = new cpppoly.VBaseArgs<int>(5);
    if (thunkH.a() != 5)                           return 1044;
    delete thunkH;
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 1)              return 1045;

    // DISCRIMINATOR: as a CFlat struct FIELD. The PRE binary compiles this and segfaults on the
    // first member call, because the field is left unconstructed.
    cpppoly.reset_vbase_dtors();
    {
        ThunkHolder thunkF = default;
        if (thunkF.a.t() != 107)                   return 1046;
        if (thunkF.a.a() != 1)                     return 1047;
    }
    if (cpppoly.vbase_dtors() != 1)              return 1048;

